<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Notification Service Extension entitlements.

  The two group entries are IDENTICAL to Nedwons.entitlements, and that is the entire point of this
  file: an extension has its own bundle identifier, so without explicit shared groups it gets its
  own private container and its own private Keychain. It would then find no MLS store and no
  session, and every contentless push would fall back to the generic "New message" wake — silently,
  on device only, with nothing in the logs to say why.

  The extension deliberately holds NO capabilities of its own. It does not push, does not attest,
  and never registers for remote notifications; it only reads what the app already wrote.
  `aps-environment` and the App Attest entitlement belong to the app target alone.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
    <array>
        <string>group.app.nedwons.demo</string>
    </array>
    <key>keychain-access-groups</key>
    <array>
        <string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)app.nedwons.shared</string>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
